      "body": "# Description\n\nReject receive capacities that differ from the process's NCCL EP bootstrap signature before dispatch. The existing guard rejects larger capacities but accidentally permits smaller ones, contrary to its error message and the documented exact-match requirement. Keep the existing upper-bound check for the send token count.\n\nThe pinned NCCL EP dependency [rejects a receive buffer smaller than its fixed dispatch budget](https://github.com/NVIDIA/nccl-extensions/blob/809f71604370c9fcc3dd8fab260d62e2b65d5152/nccl_ep/nccl_ep.cc#L4667-L4672). This changes early validation, not kernel behavior or performance.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n\n## Changes\n\n- Require `recv_capacity_per_rank == b_recv_pr` in the bootstrap compatibility guard.\n- Add five host-side regression cases: smaller/larger receive capacity, smaller/equal send token count, and an excessive send token count.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Repository pre-commit checks on both changed files: passed (clang-format not applicable).\n- Repository copyright/license checker on the new file: passed.\n- Component execution of the complete source guard and the five regression functions: baseline 4/5, fixed 5/5. The failing baseline case is the smaller receive capacity, which does not raise. This was isolated host-function execution, **not** an installed JAX/TE or NCCL run.\n- `python -m pytest -c tests/jax/pytest.ini -q tests/jax/test_moe_bootstrap.py`: blocked at `conftest.py` import because this Windows environment has no `jax`. Full JAX/L0 and GPU/distributed tests have not been run.\n\nKept as Draft pending human-author review and the configured JAX CI environment, as required by this repository's agent contribution policy.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the contributing guidelines.\n- [x] I have added regression tests.\n- [ ] New and existing unit tests pass locally through the installed frontend.\n- [ ] All applicable L0 checks pass.\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
